title: Files open in tabs one after the other (each right after the one in front), a tab is brought to the front by its number, and closing the one in front brings the one next to it
folders: rust-small
limit: 50
forbid-log: WARN.*script
forbid-log: script: ignoring
expect-log: opened .*main\.rs in a tab
expect-log: tabs: \[.*main\.rs, .*util\.rs, .*steps\.rs\], in front: Some\(2\)
expect-log: tabs: \[.*main\.rs, .*util\.rs, .*steps\.rs\], in front: Some\(0\)
expect-log: tabs: \[.*util\.rs, .*steps\.rs\], in front: Some\(0\)
expect-log: tabs: \[[^,]*util\.rs\], in front: Some\(0\)
expect-log: tabs: \[\], in front: None

wait 3000
tab open src/main.rs
wait 800
tab open src/util.rs
wait 800
tab open src/steps.rs
wait 1000
mark three-tabs
wait 450
tab report
tab front 1
wait 800
mark first-in-front
wait 450
tab report
tab close
wait 800
mark first-closed
wait 450
tab report
tab close 2
wait 800
tab report
tab close
wait 1000
mark all-closed-canvas-back
wait 450
tab report
quit
